My Changes: I added dynamic data in the myProfile section and the myInformation section of the profile. Andrew had this before, but because I needed to separate out all the pages into individual pages, I had to delete his code to get it finished.

This ticket is to make up for that. I redid the code in a more modular way. In the `profile.js` file I'm getting the profile of my user. I ONLY did this portion since this was the only code I had to delete. This is done by the following:

```JavaScript
export async function getStaticProps() {
    const prisma = new PrismaClient()
    const profile = await prisma.user.findMany({
        where: {
            id: {
                equals: 1
            }
        },
    })
    
    return {
      props : { profile }
    };
}
```

Please note, that where I have `id equal to 1` **THIS WILL HAVE TO CHANGE LATER**. I'm only doing this now, but to get that, we would have to be passing the id when the user session starts, maybe store the id into a session which will be done in the future. 

I'm getting the information in `myProfile` and `myInformation` cards by passing the `profile` property. I can access the data like so:

```JavaScript
            {profile.map((user) => (
                <div key = {user.id}>
                         {user.fname} // Prints the first name in the table
                </div>
            ))}
```
